WEBVTT

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.000
The musical department has gotten a request.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.790
They asked us to send volunteer staff

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:42.200
who could use the practical training
to help with a pamphlet photoshoot.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.870
Does that mean we can
see professionals at work?

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.200
That's amazing!

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.790
Why would you ask us to do it?

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:56.000
It would be a valuable experience, so
the Kao Council wants to give it to first years.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.910
And so, I decided to have the five of you go.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:08.500
That was an unexpectedly
lucky invitation to the ball.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.450
There was an amazing prince waiting
for us at the castle where we were heading.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.330
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:31.660
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:38.830
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:46.660
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.160
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:54.700
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:02.950
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:09.200
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.250
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:17.750
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.450
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:27.200
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.410
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:32.870
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:36.410
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.910
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:52.200
"Act 11"

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.830
Wow... It's like we're...

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.160
We're really out of place.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.910
Don't get nervous, Nayuki.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.040
The actor's coming in!

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.540
Ladies and gentlemen, thanks for waiting!

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.660
He is the main actor of the company,
the hero of this stage--

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.750
Ladies are in love with him,
gentlemen bow down to him.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:26.120
He is the musical prince
flourishing in the moment--

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.700
Haruto Tsukigami!

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.250
♪ The time is ripe ♪

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:59.330
♪ Put on the veil ♪

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.540
♪ Noble man ♪

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.870
♪ The emperor, swooping down ♪

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:15.700
♪ Let the symphony playing
in our hearts ring out ♪

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:22.790
♪ Because even an ordinary
night can turn into a miracle ♪

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:27.200
♪ What a beautiful thing, a serenade ♪

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.540
♪ An escaping smile ♪

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:37.620
♪ Tragedy, comedy, and even love adorns ♪

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:44.250
♪ This dazzling dream ♪

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.620
H-H-Haruto?

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.370
Today is the day of the practical training, yes?

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.290
Hiragi's a strange man.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:22.910
If it were me, I would have given such a
wonderful opportunity to my own students.

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.330
He isn't motivated by self-interest.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:28.580
That has always been
one of Hiragi's good traits.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:30.120
<i>Oui</i> .

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.080
How can you be so calm?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.620
Why did he give the opportunity
to the team Otori left behind?

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.250
Aren't you being too suspicious?

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:45.830
It's the team Tsukigami's little brother
is in, so he was just being considerate.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:50.290
Hiragi, have you still not come to your senses?

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.870
After we went through all
that trouble of keeping him away...

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:59.000
Akatsuki, are your actions really
for the best interest of the school?

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.080
What did you say?

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:05.330
You did not just incite us
because of your hate for Otori, did you?

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:12.370
I just picked a poisonous flower that
was blooming in the Ayanagi garden...

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:17.040
...in order to protect the most
noble and beautiful flower of all.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.750
"King Edward"
"Starring Haruto Tsukigami &amp; Rin Harukaze"

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.700
Hiragi had an interesting idea.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.160
I never thought he'd send <i>you</i> , Kaito.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.040
You didn't encourage him to do it, did you?

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.080
The editor is the one who thought of this!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.660
In order to create buzz
since I'm an Ayanagi alum.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:46.910
If it's uncomfortable for you,
you can leave early.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.870
I'll talk to the staff and the school.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.500
That's not for me to decide.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.660
Our team leader is Hoshitani.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:07:03.160
That's unexpected. You've almost always
been the leader of the groups you're in.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:09.450
That was just because I was angry and
obsessed with being at the top of my class.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:10.950
But now...

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:17.410
You seem to be enjoying your life
at school in your own way, Kaito.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.410
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:23.080
The costume's ready! Haruto, if you will.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.080
Coming!

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.870
Off you go.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.410
Thanks.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:33.790
I saw that, little Kaito.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:38.540
Even if you're usually aloof,
you're cute when you're with your brother.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:42.000
Lucky. I want a big brother, too.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.750
You guys!

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.540
Don't snoop.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.580
Boys, we're starting!

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.200
Y-Yes, sir!

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.950
We're going for a serious mood.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.250
Try resting your chin in your hand like this.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:06.330
Can you bring a slight smile to your lips? Like
you're looking down on someone.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:10.330
Should I be more provoking?

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:11.660
Wanna put a hickey on your neck?

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.750
If it'll make the audience happy,
I'll do what I can.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:17.410
I'm sure they'll like it.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:19.750
All right, why don't you try drawing your sword?

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.620
Get some wind on him! Make his hair move.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.540
Did Tsukigami lose weight?

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:32.250
He said he got toned because
Western armor makes you look fatter.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:34.410
Haruto's so stoic!

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.160
Pros really are amazing.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.910
I hate to admit it, but he's impressive.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:47.040
It's not often that you get a chance to
see something like this with your own eyes.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.330
We have to thank Hiragi.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:55.250
Hoshitani?

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:56.700
Haruto, sir!

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:57.950
Good work back there!

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:00.290
Thanks, woah, for today...

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:04.540
No, thank you. I feel bad keeping you from your practice.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:04.540
Oh, excuse me... It's all right.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:08.410
Is your preparation for the
Ayanagi Festival going well?

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:12.410
Yes, we are working hard...

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:16.500
Oh, are you worried about something?

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:21.700
Um, how can I lead the team better?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:22.790
What?

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.950
Watching you work, I thought it was amazing.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:31.000
You were shining and making
everyone have a good time...

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.950
It seemed like you weren't worried
or discouraged about anything.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:38.910
At first, there was plenty
I was worried and discouraged about.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:42.000
But I had to get over that
before the performance.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.660
How did you do it?

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:49.000
Even though I'm the one who
has to lead the team as the leader,

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:53.410
I don't even know how to make <i>myself</i> shine...

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.620
You're still a student.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.660
You still have time to learn how to do that.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:07.290
But it's not my job to teach you how to do it.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:10.580
I hope your performance at
the Ayanagi Festival is a success.

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:25.290
One, two, three, four!

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:34.080
We made it to the end!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.910
We've somehow managed to complete it.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.370
I hope the audience likes it!

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:40.750
We're not done yet.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.660
We have to practice it over
and over before the performance.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:52.620
You haven't contacted Otori yet?

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.040
Kuga...

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.700
If it's too hard, I'll do it for you.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:01.160
When you're too quiet, it throws me off.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:04.620
Thanks. But it's fine!

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:08.250
Besides, we've already gotten this far.
We can do it with just the five of us!

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.580
I'll go wash my face.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:12.120
Hoshitani?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.750
That's not how his smile usually looks.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.910
Is it really all right to continue
tolerating what Otori is doing?

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.370
I think it's time to make a decision.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:33.120
Oh, Tsukigami. Thanks.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.370
There's something I wanted to tell you.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:41.500
There's a possibility
I've been thinking about for a while...

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:44.580
About why Otori left...

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:52.450
That is correct, more or less.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:57.580
I told Otori that we were going to cancel
your performance at the Ayanagi Festival.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:00.080
But he refused to accept that.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:04.120
He asked that you boys be allowed to
perform in exchange for his own resignation,

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:06.580
as the one who formed the team
in the first place and taught you.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:10.500
Why... Why did you allow that?

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:14.450
Isn't he your relative? Aren't you friends?

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:16.000
Hoshitani!

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.950
No, that's not it...

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:20.950
It's our fault...

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:25.660
For our sakes, Otori...

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:27.120
Hey!

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.040
Man, I can't believe you.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.160
Don't just rush out like that.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.700
What's the point in causing
trouble for Hiragi, too?

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.950
I didn't know anything...

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:45.660
I... didn't know anything...

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.450
I'm in the same boat.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:50.370
And so is everyone else...

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:54.540
I want to talk to him properly one more time...

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.700
I want to see Otori again...!

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.830
"You have a new message"

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:23.830
Hey, boy.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.580
Otori...

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:33.660
An actor smiles when he wants to cry.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:41.160
Why... Why did you leave
without saying anything?

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:45.080
How could you decide something
so important on your own?

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:49.950
We were able to make it this far
because you were with us, sir.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:52.580
It's wrong for you to sacrifice yourself for us.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.910
I can't accept it!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:57.330
Then, if I return to the Kao Council,

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.910
will you give up on performing
at the Ayanagi Festival in exchange?

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:06.450
If your feelings are that fickle,
then you shouldn't perform.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:10.080
You wouldn't be able to put on
a decent performance, anyway.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:13.540
I'd feel bad for the audience watching you.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.700
Our feelings <i>aren't</i> that fickle!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.290
We're--

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:24.500
Remember what you're aiming for. Your dream.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:28.870
Is it to stay by my side forever?

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.330
I...

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:36.830
My dream is...

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:42.910
♪ Stride of a star ♪

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:46.660
♪ Always... ♪

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:47.120
♪ The first step of the beginning ♪

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:49.910
♪ Be with you ♪

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:51.330
♪ I'll make tomorrow's smile shine ♪

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:58.040
♪ So that it'll reach that dazzling place ♪

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.870
♪ I won't give up ♪

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:19.540
♪ I'll even use the pain ♪

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.040
♪ Break through the wall ♪

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:26.750
♪ I'll place my bets on a
possibility that's not zero ♪

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.660
♪ Keep on try ♪

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:27.830
♪ It's like a shooting star! ♪

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:35.450
♪ When light shone on my too-average days ♪

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:33.450
♪ From here ♪

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:42.120
♪ I'll take the steps I decided in my heart ♪

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:39.700
♪ To the beyond ♪

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.120
♪ Fly away ♪

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:46.120
♪ To the new world ♪

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.950
♪ Believe in myself! ♪

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:54.910
♪ Even if I stumble, my toes are facing forward ♪

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:58.700
♪ Even when I reflect on it, I don't regret it ♪

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.950
♪ Go for it! ♪

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:58.700
♪ That's all right! ♪

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:02.290
♪ My heart's beating faster, infinitely ♪

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:08.200
-♪ Stride of a star ♪

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.620
♪ Stride of a star ♪

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:11.450
♪ Admiration draws the map of courage ♪

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:12.620
♪ Today, as well ♪

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:16.620
♪ That leads me to the future ♪

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:26.200
♪ The twinkling of my heart
is released into the sky ♪

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:44.000
I was able to come to Ayanagi Academy
because of that high schooler,

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:52.040
but you're the one who taught me that
singing, acting, and dancing can be this fun, sir.

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:57.660
I want a lot of people to watch the
performance you taught the five of us.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:01.330
That's my... <i>our</i> dream!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.950
I definitely don't want to give up on it.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.870
That's why...

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.580
...you will abandon me.

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:11.040
Yes, sir.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:20.790
Let me enjoy myself until the end, boys.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.950
According to the Japan Meteorological Agency,

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:06.910
the approaching typhoon is predicted
to stay strong as it makes landfall.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:10.790
The atmospheric pressure near the
center is approximately 940 hectopascals...

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:15.580
"Ayanagi Festival"

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.580
"Ayanagi Festival"

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.580
"Ayanagi Festival Day 1 Program"

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.950
The adjustments we made seem fine.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:31.700
They're flawless.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:34.660
You didn't deliver the goods
at the last minute this time, huh?

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:36.620
Good job, Nayuki Sisters!

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:38.040
Hey, stop that!

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:40.160
Pervert.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:42.160
Now, now, Tengenji.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.870
Well, we'll be watching from
the audience, so do your best!

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:48.870
Don't get nervous, bro!

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.830
Full speed ahead!

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.200
Yeah, thanks.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.370
I'll go with them until they
get out of the school building.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.370
It's dangerous with all the guys around.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:18:59.160
Oh my!

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:01.120
We'll be invincible!

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.370
I'll go pick up the catering.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.540
We should eat a little something.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.540
Let's go, Tengenji.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.870
Don't tell me what to do, you boor!

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:12.200
Thanks!

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:19.370
Oh, the wind's gotten
really strong, huh, Nayuki--?!

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:27.040
An actor smiles when he wants to cry, right?

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:33.160
Don't worry. Everyone'll be with you.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:35.540
Me too, for what it's worth.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:41.040
You've gotten very dependable, Hoshitani.

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:44.910
It's not that you haven't
been dependable until now.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.910
It's just that even though
we were called a motley bunch,

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:51.910
the five of us worked hard together,

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:55.790
but if you hadn't been there, Hoshitani,

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.830
I don't think we would have
become the team we are now.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:04.040
N-Nayuki...?

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.250
S-Sorry...

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:08.950
Huh? I wonder why I'm...

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:13.500
I guess I just remembered some things...

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:16.700
The day we first met...

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:22.200
The day you first talked to
Tengenji and he got mad at you...

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.290
The day we shared our lunch with Kuga...

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:28.910
The day we got in a
fight because of Tsukigami...

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:34.830
A lot of stuff has happened, but you're
the one who brought us all together...

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:37.910
I... I didn't do anything...

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:40.750
That's why I want to apologize.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:44.830
I thought... maybe if it was you...

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:50.660
Maybe if it was you,
you'd pull the weak me along.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:55.660
Maybe if it was you, you wouldn't
let go of my hand halfway through...

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:59.620
I always felt guilty that
I was trying to size you up.

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:06.750
But being near your kindness and fun,
I even forgot those feelings.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:11.790
That's how dazzling you are to me, Hoshitani.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:19.700
You know what?
I really, really love you, Hoshitani!

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:25.790
Me too! I like you and everyone else!

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:29.000
I love Team Otori!

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.790
You know what?

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.040
I'm glad we ended up with these team members.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.580
Yeah.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.950
Let's have fun with
everything we've got today...

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:42.830
...at our performance!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:22:01.200
<i>Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams</i>

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:07.700
<i>On a night when you look up at a starless sky</i>

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:11.200
<i>Just remember (today)</i>

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:15.500
<i>The days we ran like crazy (together)</i>

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:19.620
<i>Those steps were miracles</i>

00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:22.870
<i>Ring out, Countdown!</i>

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:26.500
<i>Taking off for the future from here</i>

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:30.450
<i>You will start singing again</i>

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:33.620
<i>There are things you lack</i>

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:37.500
<i>So you reach out desperately to grab them</i>

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:41.000
<i>These hot, passionate feelings overflowing</i>

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.750
<i>Make the light of the stars your ally</i>

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:48.290
<i>Even bluffing can become your pride</i>

00:22:48.290 --> 00:22:51.950
<i>You can fly however you want</i>

00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:57.950
<i>Everything starts now!</i>

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:24.200
Oh no!

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:26.290
It looks like the outdoor stage collapsed!

00:23:26.290 --> 00:23:28.500
Seriously?

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.660
Collapsed?

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:33.580
This is a message from the Kao Council.

00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:37.290
Members of the Kao Council and
Ayanagi Festival committee members

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:40.540
please gather promptly in
the Ayanagi Hall meeting room.

00:23:40.540 --> 00:23:44.250
I repeat, members of the Kao Council
and Ayanagi Festival committee members...

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:46.700
The guys in charge are starting to act.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:49.330
So all we can do is wait
for their decision, huh?

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:53.870
Hoshitani!

00:23:55.790 --> 00:23:57.120
No way...

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:28.790
"Act 12"

00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:00.410
Hey, Hiragi.

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:01.450
Tsukigami, sir!

00:24:01.450 --> 00:24:03.120
Thanks for always taking
care of my little brother.

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:04.160
I haven't done anything...

00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:07.330
Don't be modest. It looks
like you've done a lot for him.

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:08.410
Tsukigami, sir?

00:24:08.410 --> 00:24:11.450
Next time, let me take the
time to settle things with you.

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:13.790
Oh, there were unavoidable
circumstances that were in no way--

00:24:13.790 --> 00:24:28.790
"Hiragi"
